-- title:
--   Original BV compact stopped compensated-jump and signed HJB budget under strategy alone
-- statement:
--   For the original BV Levy process and its original filtration, every bounded right-continuous stopped clock and predictable positive-reserve compact event have an integrable centred nonlinear negative-jump compensation and an integrable nonpositive expected HJB drift, requiring only the actual original dividend strategy. This strengthens the previous admissibility-based P3-E2 compact budget so that a positively shifted starting reserve can be used on the genuine unshifted ruin clock without assuming shifted admissibility. The hypothesis remains a strictly positive compact reserve band; lower-boundary passage and stopped cash/ruin dividend ledger remain to be proved. No global L1 of the unlocalised signed generator is assumed.

